<section style="padding:80px 0 32px;">
  <div class="max-site" style="max-width:760px;">
    <span class="eyebrow" style="font-size:18px; display:block; margin-bottom:14px;">Provisions,</span>
    <h1 class="display" style="font-size:60px; line-height:1.04; margin:0; letter-spacing:-0.018em;">Privacy <em style="color:var(--color-clay);">policy.</em></h1>
    <p style="font-family:var(--font-display); font-style:italic; font-size:17px; color:var(--color-ink-faded); margin:18px 0 0;">Effective date: April 23, 2026</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section style="padding:32px 0 96px;">
  <div class="max-site harbor-legal" style="max-width:760px;">
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy describes how Craft &amp; Ship, operated by Craft &amp; Ship LLC ("Craft &amp; Ship,"
        "we," "us," or "our"), collects, uses, and protects your personal information when you use
        our service ("Service") at craftandship.io. By using the Service, you agree
        to the practices described in this policy.
      </p>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-100 mb-3">1. Information We Collect</h2>

        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-100 mt-5 mb-3">Information you provide directly</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 pl-5 list-disc marker:text-subtle">
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">Account information:</strong> name, email address, and password (stored as a bcrypt hash; we never store your plaintext password)</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">Website specifications:</strong> the written specification we draw up from your conversation, and the descriptions and requirements in it</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">Conversations:</strong> every message you exchange with Haven, our AI companion, and with the other chats on this site where you describe your website, is stored. This starts with your first message, before you have an account: until then the conversation is tied to a cookie in your browser. Messages to the support chat are sent to us to be answered and are not stored on our servers; your browser keeps them until you close the tab</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">Notes from your conversation:</strong> from what you tell Haven we keep short notes about you and your work, which she uses in later replies</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">Messages that suggest a crisis:</strong> if a message suggests that you or someone else may be in danger, it is stored like any other, and a notice that it happened, without the text of your message, is emailed to the person who runs this site</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">Payment information:</strong> processed and stored by Stripe; we do not store your full credit card number, only a Stripe customer ID and payment references</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-100 mt-5 mb-3">Information collected automatically</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 pl-5 list-disc marker:text-subtle">
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">Usage logs:</strong> build status, timestamps, and technical metadata about your website builds</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">Page views:</strong> for each page you open we record its address, the address of the page that linked you here, any campaign tags in the link, and your session and account identifiers when you have them. For a conversation with Haven we also record a one-way hash of your browser's user-agent string, which we use to tell people from automated visitors. If you send us feedback through the feedback form, the page you were on and your browser's user-agent string are stored with it</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">Cookies:</strong> see the Cookies section below</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-gray-100 mt-5 mb-3">Information we do not collect</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 pl-5 list-disc marker:text-subtle">
          <li>We do not use advertising trackers, or cookies that follow you to other sites</li>
          <li>We do not collect location data, and we do not store your IP address in our database. We do store the address of the page that linked you to us and the user-agent hash described above</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-100 mb-3">2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-2 pl-5 list-disc marker:text-subtle">
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">To provide the Service:</strong> processing your website specifications, building your websites, and deploying them</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">To communicate with you:</strong> sending build status notifications, account-related emails, a short series of welcome and follow-up emails, and responding to support requests</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">To process payments:</strong> facilitating transactions through Stripe</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">To improve the Service:</strong> we count page views and how far conversations get. Once a week, recent messages from conversations with Haven (never ones flagged as a crisis) are read by an AI model to draft answers to questions that come up often, and the support chat may give those answers to other customers. A draft that contains a link, markup or an email address is discarded; nobody reviews the rest before it is used</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">To protect the Service:</strong> detecting and preventing fraud, abuse, and security threats</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-100 mb-3">3. Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          We share information with the following third-party services as necessary to operate the
          platform. Each service processes data according to its own privacy policy:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 pl-5 list-disc marker:text-subtle">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-100">Stripe</strong> (payments): processes your payment information, and receives your email address when you start a subscription.
            <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand hover:underline hover:text-brand-sky">Stripe Privacy Policy</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-100">Railway</strong> (hosting): hosts this site and its database, where everything described in this policy is stored, and hosts your websites.
            <a href="https://railway.app/legal/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand hover:underline hover:text-brand-sky">Railway Privacy Policy</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-100">Resend</strong> (email): delivers every email we send you (account emails, build notifications, the welcome and follow-up emails), and carries a message you send through the contact form to us.
            <a href="https://resend.com/legal/privacy-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand hover:underline hover:text-brand-sky">Resend Privacy Policy</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-100">Anthropic</strong> (AI): Haven's replies are written by Anthropic's Claude. Each message you send her goes to Anthropic's API together with the recent conversation and the notes kept from it, to write the reply, to decide which notes to keep, and, when you ask for your website, to turn the conversation into a structured website specification. Messages in the support chat and in the other chats on this site are sent the same way, and build and deployment logs may be sent for diagnostics. The website itself is assembled from our library of pre-built building blocks and is not generated by Anthropic.
            <a href="https://www.anthropic.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand hover:underline hover:text-brand-sky">Anthropic Privacy Policy</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-100">Google Fonts</strong> (typefaces): our pages load their fonts from Google, so your browser contacts Google's servers when it opens a page.
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-brand hover:underline hover:text-brand-sky">Google Privacy Policy</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-gray-100">Services that are used only when switched on:</strong> OpenAI, which receives the notes kept from your conversation and the message you are sending, to help Haven find the notes that matter to it; Sentry, which receives reports of errors on this site (page addresses without their query strings, never the body of what you sent); and Plausible, which counts page views in your browser and sets no cookies.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">
          We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information to any third party, for advertising
          or any other purpose.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-100 mb-3">4. Cookies</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          We set two cookies, both needed for the site to work:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 pl-5 list-disc marker:text-subtle">
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">The session cookie</strong> (<code><%= cookieFacts.sessionCookieName %></code>) keeps you logged in and holds the state of forms between pages. It expires after <%= cookieFacts.sessionIdleHours %> hours without a visit, and a login ends after <%= cookieFacts.sessionMaxDays %> days however often you visit; then you log in again</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">The conversation cookie</strong> (<code><%= cookieFacts.conversationCookieName %></code>) is set when you open the conversation with Haven and is what ties that conversation to your browser before you have an account. It lasts <%= cookieFacts.conversationDays %> days from your first visit. If you start a subscription from that browser, the same cookie lets it reach your conversation and your website's page for <%= cookieFacts.conversationPaidDays %> days after the payment</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">Both cookies are:</p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 pl-5 list-disc marker:text-subtle">
          <li>HTTP-only (not accessible to JavaScript)</li>
          <li>Secure (transmitted only over HTTPS in production)</li>
          <li>SameSite: Lax (provides CSRF protection)</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">
          We do not use advertising cookies, analytics cookies, or any third-party tracking cookies.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-100 mb-3">5. Data Security</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">We take reasonable measures to protect your information, including:</p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 pl-5 list-disc marker:text-subtle">
          <li>Passwords are hashed with bcrypt before storage</li>
          <li>Connections between your browser and this site use HTTPS, with HSTS enabled</li>
          <li>CSRF protection on all state-changing operations</li>
          <li>Parameterized database queries to prevent SQL injection</li>
          <li>Security headers (Content-Security-Policy, X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options)</li>
          <li>Session data stored server-side in PostgreSQL</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">
          No method of transmission or storage is 100% secure. While we strive to protect your
          information, we cannot guarantee absolute security.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-100 mb-3">6. Data Retention</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-2 pl-5 list-disc marker:text-subtle">
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">Active accounts:</strong> your account data, website specifications, conversations and notes are kept for as long as your account exists. Nothing deletes them on a schedule, except that the records of old failed builds are cleared out automatically</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">Conversations without an account:</strong> a conversation you have with Haven before you have an account stays in our database after its cookie expires. Nothing deletes it on a schedule. Write to us and we will remove it</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">Account deletion:</strong> you can delete your account yourself, with your password, at <a href="/account/delete" class="text-brand hover:underline hover:text-brand-sky">/account/delete</a>, or ask us to. Deleting it removes, at once: your account record, your conversations with Haven and the notes kept from them, your messages in the other chats, your feedback, and the emails scheduled for you. It also tells Stripe to end any subscription at the close of the period you have paid for</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">What account deletion leaves:</strong> the records of your website builds stay in our database with the link to your account removed. They include the specification each website was built from, which holds what you told us about your work and can include your email address, and the build's logs. The log of emails we sent you, with your address, also stays, and so does an address you gave the newsletter list. Page-view records stay without your account identifier. Write to us and we will remove these by hand</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">Hosted websites:</strong> deleting your account does not take your website down, and it does not delete the website's own database. If you want the website taken down, write to us; a person does that, and we will do it within 30 days of your request</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">Anonymized data:</strong> aggregated, anonymized data that cannot identify you may be retained indefinitely for service improvement</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">Legal obligations:</strong> we may retain certain data as required by law (such as payment records for tax purposes)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-100 mb-3">7. Your Rights</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">You have the right to:</p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 pl-5 list-disc marker:text-subtle">
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">Access your data:</strong> request a copy of the personal information we hold about you. While logged in you can download your account record, your builds, your intake chat messages and your feature requests at <a href="/export-data" class="text-brand hover:underline hover:text-brand-sky">/export-data</a>; that download does not include your conversation with Haven or the notes kept from it, so write to us for those</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">Correct your data:</strong> request correction of any inaccurate information</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">Delete your data:</strong> delete your account yourself, or request deletion of your account and personal information; the Data Retention section says what deletion removes and what it leaves</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">Unsubscribe from emails:</strong> use the unsubscribe link in our emails. It stops every email from us except the ones that verify your address and reset your password, so it also stops the emails that tell you a build is ready</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">
          To exercise any of these rights, contact us at
          <a href="mailto:support@craftandship.io" class="text-brand hover:underline hover:text-brand-sky">support@craftandship.io</a>.
          We will respond to requests within 30 days.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-100 mb-3">8. California Residents (CCPA)</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          If you are a California resident, you have additional rights under the California Consumer
          Privacy Act (CCPA):
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 pl-5 list-disc marker:text-subtle">
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">Right to know:</strong> you may request details about the categories and specific pieces of personal information we have collected about you</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">Right to delete:</strong> you may request deletion of your personal information, subject to certain exceptions</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">Right to opt out of sale:</strong> we do not sell personal information, so this right does not apply</li>
          <li><strong class="text-gray-100">Non-discrimination:</strong> we will not discriminate against you for exercising your CCPA rights</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-4">
          To make a CCPA request, email us at
          <a href="mailto:support@craftandship.io" class="text-brand hover:underline hover:text-brand-sky">support@craftandship.io</a> with "CCPA Request"
          in the subject line.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-100 mb-3">9. Children's Privacy</h2>
        <p>
          The Service is not intended for anyone under the age of 18. We do not knowingly collect
          personal information from children under 18. If we become aware that we have collected
          information from a child under 18, we will take steps to delete that information promptly.
          If you believe a child under 18 has provided us with personal information, please contact
          us at <a href="mailto:support@craftandship.io" class="text-brand hover:underline hover:text-brand-sky">support@craftandship.io</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-100 mb-3">10. International Users</h2>
        <p>
          The Service is operated from the United States. If you are accessing the Service from
          outside the United States, your information will be transferred to and processed in the
          United States. By using the Service, you consent to this transfer.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-100 mb-3">11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. For material changes, we will provide
          at least 30 days advance notice via email. The "Effective Date" at the top of this page
          indicates when the policy was last updated.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-100 mb-3">12. Contact Us</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or our data practices, contact us at:
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong class="text-gray-100">Craft &amp; Ship</strong><br />
          Email: <a href="mailto:support@craftandship.io" class="text-brand hover:underline hover:text-brand-sky">support@craftandship.io</a><br />
          Texas, USA
        </p>
      </div>
  </div>
</section>

